    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "d3f3a3feac869b312e49fd2fb78a6a7a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"hypothesis\">\ud83d\udd2c Hypothesis</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Spectral feature space reveals strong vs blunted music responders that enrich MDD/Control labels.</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Expected pattern:</strong> Clusters become features for a RecSys recommending music a patient is likely to respond to.</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Music has rich spectral structure. We predict <strong>controls</strong> show elevated high-frequency power and stronger auditory\u2013limbic coherence during <em>positive music</em>. <strong>MDD</strong> (anhedonia) exhibits blunted responses.</span>\n</blockquote></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
